>element</Name><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>PushRight</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Appends a new element to the right side of the buffer (FIFO/queue enqueue operation)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>ReplaceAtIndex</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Replaces an element at a specific index with the given element]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>index</Name><Type>DINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Properties><Property><Name>TcPlcInterfaceType</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="ApplicationBase">FifoBuffer</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Provides a simplified FIFO queue interface as an adapter over AnyBuffer]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><Implements Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBufferStrategy</Implements><SubItem><Name>anyBuffer</Name><Type Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBuffer</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>isInitialized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_overwrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When TRUE, Push overwrites oldest element when full]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reversed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When TRUE, reverses push/pop direction (PushLeft/PopRight)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>Pop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes and retrieves an element from the queue (FIFO or LIFO depending on reversed setting)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Variable to receive the popped element]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisFull</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the queue is at maximum capacity

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the queue is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Use this property to check if Push operation would succeed before attempting to
add an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Queue is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: Queue has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT fifo.isFull THEN
    value := 100;
    fifo.Push(value);  // Safe to push
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisEmpty</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the queue contains no elements

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the queue is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Queue is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: Queue contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT fifo.isEmpty THEN
    fifo.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isEmpty</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Push</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Adds a new element to the queue (direction depends on reversed setting)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Element to add to the queue]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Clear</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes all elements from the queue and resets to empty state]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_TEST_AnyBuffer_Element</Name><BitSize>672</BitSize><SubItem><Name>id</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>name</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="ApplicationBase">LifoBuffer</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Provides a simplified LIFO stack interface as an adapter over AnyBuffer]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><Implements Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBufferStrategy</Implements><SubItem><Name>anyBuffer</Name><Type Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBuffer</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>isInitialized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_overwrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When TRUE, Push overwrites oldest element when full]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reversed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ When TRUE, reverses push/pop direction (PushLeft/PopLeft)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>Pop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes and retrieves an element from the stack (LIFO pop operation)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Variable to receive the popped element]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisFull</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the stack is at maximum capacity

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the stack is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Use this property to check if Push operation would succeed before attempting to
add an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Stack is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: Stack has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT lifo.isFull THEN
    value := 100;
    lifo.Push(value);  // Safe to push
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisEmpty</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the stack contains no elements

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the stack is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Stack is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: Stack contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT lifo.isEmpty THEN
    lifo.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isEmpty</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Push</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Adds a new element to the stack (LIFO push operation, direction depends on reversed setting)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Element to add to the stack]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Clear</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes all elements from the stack and resets to empty state]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="ApplicationBase">ListBuffer</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Provides a directional FIFO list with automatic shift-and-overwrite when full]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><Implements Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBufferStrategy</Implements><SubItem><Name>anyBuffer</Name><Type Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBuffer</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>isInitialized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_reversed</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE: add at left, FALSE: add at right (end)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>Pop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes and retrieves the oldest element from the list (FIFO dequeue)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Variable to receive the popped element]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisFull</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the list is at maximum capacity

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the list is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Note: Push will still succeed when isFull is TRUE by automatically removing the
oldest element and shifting remaining elements. This property is informational
and indicates when the next Push will trigger shift-and-overwrite behavior.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: List is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: List has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF list.isFull THEN
    // Next Push will remove oldest element and shift
    Trace.Info('List', 'Next push will overwrite oldest element');
END_IF

value := 100;
success := list.Push(value);  // Will succeed even if full
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisEmpty</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the list contains no elements

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the list is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: List is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: List contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT list.isEmpty THEN
    list.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isEmpty</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Push</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Adds a new element to the list with automatic shift-and-overwrite when full]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Element to add to the list]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>Clear</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes all elements from the list and resets to empty state]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize></Method><Method><Name>removeOldest</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Private helper method to remove the oldest element based on fill direction]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>dummyElement</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ For discarding oldest element]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="ApplicationBase">RingBuffer</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Provides a circular buffer (ring buffer) interface with automatic overwrite capability]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><Implements Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBufferStrategy</Implements><SubItem><Name>anyBuffer</Name><Type Namespace="ApplicationBase">I_AnyBuffer</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>isInitialized</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>_overwrite</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE: overwrites oldest when full]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>200</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><Method><Name>Pop</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Removes and retrieves the oldest element from the ring buffer (FIFO dequeue)]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>element</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Variable to receive the popped element]]></Comment><Type>AnyType</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>anytypeclass</Name><Value>ANY</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>hasanytype</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisFull</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the ring buffer is at maximum capacity

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the ring buffer is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Note: When overwriteEnabled is TRUE, Push will still succeed even when isFull is TRUE
by automatically removing the oldest element. When overwriteEnabled is FALSE, Push
will fail when isFull is TRUE.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Ring buffer is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: Ring buffer has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF ring.isFull THEN
    // With overwriteEnabled=TRUE, Push will overwrite oldest
    // With overwriteEnabled=FALSE, Push will fail
    value := 100;
    success := ring.Push(value);
END_IF
```
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Local><Name>isFull</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Local><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getisEmpty</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns TRUE if the ring buffer contains no elements

## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the ring buffer is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Ring buffer is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: Ring buffer contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT ring.isEmpty THEN
    ring.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
